{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeqWv6Z4c7Wfxxf8rQjBh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have everything I need. Here's the full picture.\n\n## Why isolation fails\n\n**\"The data directory\" is actually three directories, resolved from three independent knobs, and `WORKLOG_DIR` only moves one of them.**\n\n| Directory | What lives there | How it's resolved | Documented? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Worklog dir | WORK.md, notes/, archive/, FEEDBACK.md (markdown projections) | `--dir` flag, then `$WORKLOG_DIR` (`root.go:81-89`) | Yes — help text and README both call it \"the worklog data directory\" |\n| Store dir | `worklog.db` — the SQLite **source of truth** | `$WORKLOG_MIGRATION_DATA`, else `~/.local/share/worklog-migration` (`task_store.go:174`) | No — appears in no help text or README |\n| Devboard dir | `devboard/<repo>/<slug>.yaml` projections | `$DEVBOARD_DATA`, else `~/.local/share/devboard` (`devboard.go:221`) | Only in `worklog serve --help` |\n\nThe sequence when the colleague pointed `WORKLOG_DIR` at a fresh directory:\n\n1. Every write verb goes through `openStoreForWrite` (`store_common.go:110`), which opens the store at `storeDataDir()` — **still the shared, fully-populated default DB**, so the `requireAdopted` guard passes and nothing hints that the store didn't move.\n2. It then runs the hand-edit guard, `projection.EditedIn`, comparing what the *shared* store renders against the files in the *fresh* `WORKLOG_DIR`.\n3. `EditedIn` deliberately treats an absent file as an edit — \"A rendered file missing from disk counts as edited; it was deleted\" (`projection.go:187`, `:201-212`). In a fresh directory every projection is absent, so every one is reported as \"edited by hand,\" listing files the colleague never touched.\n\nI reproduced it exactly with this session's scratch setup: `WORKLOG_DIR=<fresh mktemp dir> worklog note wl-scratch-isolation \"test\"` → exit 1, `refusing to write … FEEDBACK.md, WORK.md`. Tellingly, isolating *this* session correctly required setting all three env vars — the harness that set up my environment had to know the undocumented ones.\n\nTwo aggravating details:\n\n- **The error's advice is actively anti-isolation.** \"Reconcile them first (they are build outputs; the store is the source)\" means re-render — which would pour the shared store's real data into the scratch dir. And if `DEVBOARD_DATA` is unset, any write that did proceed would render board YAML into the *real* `~/.local/share/devboard`. One knob moved, two didn't: you get cross-contamination, not isolation.\n- **The codebase already recognized the mirror-image bug and fixed only that side.** The comment on `requireAdopted` (`store_common.go:72-81`) describes almost this exact failure — empty store vs. populated corpus producing \"edited by hand … on a machine where nobody edited anything,\" with advice that \"is actively dangerous\" — and fixed it for the missing-*DB* case. The missing-*corpus* case (populated DB, fresh projection dir) was left with the same wrong message and the same dangerous advice.\n\nHistorically this is migration debt: `WORKLOG_MIGRATION_DATA` was a freeze-window migration knob (`TestMigrateSharesRuntimeStorePath`, `migrate_test.go:161-166`) that quietly became the runtime source-of-truth knob after cutover, while the docs kept describing the pre-store world where the markdown *was* the data and `WORKLOG_DIR` really did move everything.\n\n## Recommendations\n\n1. **Make `WORKLOG_DIR`/`--dir` the single root it's documented to be.** Derive the other two by default: store at `$WORKLOG_DIR/store/` (or similar) and devboard as a subdirectory — `projection.SingleRoot` (`projection.go:116`) shows the layout already exists for tests and staged copies. Keep `WORKLOG_MIGRATION_DATA`/`DEVBOARD_DATA` as advanced overrides for split installs, but only as overrides of a root that moves together. The subtlety: existing installs have the store at `~/.local/share/worklog-migration` with `WORKLOG_DIR` defaulted, so the default-path lookup needs to keep finding that (or a one-time relocation), while an *explicit* `--dir`/`WORKLOG_DIR` should resolve everything under the given root.\n\n2. **Until then (and as defense in depth), make the guard diagnose the fresh-dir case truthfully.** `EditedIn` can distinguish \"every projection is absent\" from \"some files differ\": an entirely-absent corpus is an unrendered directory, not a hand-edit spree. `openStoreForWrite` should refuse with an accurate message — \"this worklog dir has never been rendered; the store is at <path>, which is outside it — set WORKLOG_MIGRATION_DATA/DEVBOARD_DATA for an isolated dir, or run `worklog adopt`\" — exactly the pattern `requireAdopted` established for the sibling failure.\n\n3. **Give scratch dirs a first-class bootstrap.** A `worklog init <dir>` (or `adopt` against an empty corpus rooted at the new dir) that creates an empty store *inside* the new root and renders the empty projections. That's the workflow the colleague actually wanted, in one command.\n\n4. **Fix the docs regardless.** `worklog --help` and the README (line 156) present `WORKLOG_DIR` as \"where the data tree lives\"; neither mentions that the source of truth answers to a different, entirely undocumented variable. Even a one-line \"isolation requires all three: WORKLOG_DIR, WORKLOG_MIGRATION_DATA, DEVBOARD_DATA\" would have saved the colleague's afternoon."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3835,"cache_read_input_tokens":56464,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3835},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"17dc1d64-f036-40f4-b7b4-ba080dcec9e5","uuid":"5d9a421e-6d01-445d-a8a0-5d3e28c88dfa","timestamp":"2026-09-08T06:42:16.670Z","request_id":"req_011CeqWv49T5xx2gxSSnDiJD"}
